致虚极，　   　Attain the utmost in Passivity,
守静笃。　   　Hold firm to the basis of Quietude.
万物并作，　   The myriad things take shape and rise to activity,
吾以观复。   　But I watch them fall back to their repose.
夫物芸芸，　   Like vegetation that luxuriantly grows
各复归其根。   But returns to the root (soil) from which it springs.
归根曰静，　To return to the root is Repose;
静曰复命。　It is called going back to one's Destiny.
复命曰常，　Going back to one's Destiny is to find the Eternal Law.
知常曰明。　To know the Eternal Law is Enlightenment.
不知常，    　 　And not to know the Eternal Law
妄作，凶。　Is to court disaster.
知常容，   　　He who knows the Eternal Law is tolerant;
容乃公，   　　Being tolerant, he is impartial;
公乃王，   　　Being impartial, he is kingly;
王乃天，   　　Being kingly, he is in accord with Nature;
天乃道，   　　Being in accord with Nature, he is in accord with Tao;
道乃久，   　　Being in accord with Tao, he is eternal,
殁身不殆。　And his whole life is preserved from harm.
